# Some core loaders (Emscripten's lazy-file XHR path) probe Accept-Ranges and, if it
# says "bytes", fetch large files in byte-range chunks instead of one plain GET.
# Cloudflare's edge is documented to sometimes answer the *first* ranged request for
# a not-yet-cached resource with the full file (200) instead of the requested slice
# (206) — which this lazy-loader has no way to detect, so it treats those full-file
# bytes as if they were just the small chunk it asked for, corrupting the core's
# virtual filesystem reads with no visible error (the core still starts and runs;
# it just reads garbage). Declaring no range support here (a valid HTTP value, not a
# removal) makes Emscripten's own feature probe skip byte-range requests entirely for
# these files and fall back to a single plain GET, which has no such failure mode.
/cores/*
  Accept-Ranges: none
